 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T16:45+08:00",
 "answer": "If you mean **Singapore’s PSI**, the two labels may be measuring different things. The official **PSI is based on pollutant levels over the past 24 hours**, so it can still say *Moderate* after pollution has risen recently. Your app may be showing a more current reading or calculating an **AQI** using different data and category thresholds. The two labels aren’t necessarily a contradiction. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/our-services/pollution-control/air-pollution/faqs?trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block))\n\nFor a decision about **going outside now**, check the **1-hour PM₂.₅ reading** for your area alongside the PSI. Also check that both screens show the same location and update time. If you tell me the app name and the two readings, I can help pinpoint the difference. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/our-services/pollution-control/air-pollution/faqs?trk=article-ssr-frontend-pulse_little-text-block))",
